{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere","id":1378719,"title":"Predator question - How to be a Consensualist as a Tremere?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-05T04:23:40-07:00","id":1378719,"title":"Predator question - How to be a Consensualist as a Tremere?","content":"I'm playing a Tremere character in a discord game set in the 1960s in Asia. <br /> He is an academic type with a goodish personality. <br /> <br /> Im thinking of going with the scene queen predator type and have him feed on members of a university, but I'm also really drawn to the Consensualist predator type, given the personality I have for this character. He is basically a good person when compared to most kindred. <br /> <br /> I'm just not sure how to rp and make the Consensualist predator work tho. Can he just tell people he wants to feed off them and just make them forget it with dominate?<br /> <br /> Is the Consensualist a very inconvenient predator type to rp? Given that the coterie could be traveling all over the place?<br /> <br /> Any advice or suggestions would be most welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T05:08:05-07:00","id":1378729,"title":"","content":"How the Tremere have fallen...<br /> <br /> Dominate/Blood bonds- So long as they say yes, it's fine, right? Maybe they're just taking advantage of the Clan's herd and don't know better, Maybe you've got some wanna-be and you've told them you'll turn them eventually but for now they need to be drank from.<br /> <br /> Second option: Money. Tremere have money. Pay people for your weird kink.<br /> <br /> Third option is to feed like any other kind of vampire consentualist. Go offer the Junkies in a drug den or the party kids on the beach another way to get high. Start a blood sharing cult among mortals that you just happen to be involved in. <br /> <br /> <br /> Predator types aren't realistic. You're not going to soley feed one way through your unlife, it's at best a preference and at worst you pick what's mechanically best and then start the game by moving away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T05:18:29-07:00","id":1378732,"title":"","content":"&quot;Is the Concensualist inconvenient?&quot; Understatement of the century.<br /> <br /> The best way to pull this off is to have a herd that's always with you and you can feed on at will. Going out to feed on random people is... unlikely, extremely time consuming and considered Masquerade-breach-y. Having to convince people that 1) you're a vampire, and 2) to risk their lives so you can eat them is going to be tricky without a large amount of trust between you and the target and no disciplines. Even the people that are willing will often require more time than a standard feeding roll.<br /> <br /> Consentualists work best when you can create a group of Bella-types that are interested in you over the long term. Consentualists are gardeners and farmers, not hunters and predators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T06:54:24-07:00","id":1378747,"title":"","content":"Every situation when you are about to feed I guess make a deal with the target. Convince them to donate their blood to your mouth, maybe in exchange for money or help in the Academic department, and then erase their memory of it. Its inconvenient and tough but I mean if it works its less of a guilt issue. Salubri probably do similar without the memory loss though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit<br /> Other idea, less of a masquerade breach but still touching upon it, make a deal with people for their blood, don't say you will drink but tell them its for Occult research because you are a weirdo, and technically its probably true if your a Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  more 04-05-2020, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T09:48:00-07:00","id":1378782,"title":"","content":"V5 Predator types don't make sense to me still. This one the most. &quot;Consensualist&quot; is a major redflag for a Masquerade breach. At best you'd better cultivate Ghoul.. Anything else I don't really know. Being shoehorned into one feeding style in V5 is mind-boggling to me anyway and doesn't make sense. Not only that since your in Asia, its going to be VERY hard for you to convince random people if you can &quot;have their blood&quot; as a foreigner outright. Thats how you get reported to the police, getting on the radar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T10:20:08-07:00","id":1378785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1378782#post1378782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 Predator types don't make sense to me still. This one the most. &quot;Consensualist&quot; is a major redflag for a Masquerade breach. At best you'd better cultivate Ghoul.. Anything else I don't really know. Being shoehorned into one feeding style in V5 is mind-boggling to me anyway and doesn't make sense. Not only that since your in Asia, its going to be VERY hard for you to convince random people if you can &quot;have their blood&quot; as a foreigner outright. Thats how you get reported to the police, getting on the radar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you aren't shoe horned into one feeding style. It's your characters preferred method of feeding which most characters will have, but you can feed in other ways.<br /> <br /> As for the consensualist element, there's a few different ways to play it. You could say you need a blood donation, you could outright ask to drink from people, you could play it up as a kink thing. Of course, the ethics of getting consent and then dominating away their memory of doing it does make it a bit more ethically murky but I could see an argument for allowing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T11:31:58-07:00","id":1378812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1378785#post1378785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you aren't shoe horned into one feeding style. It's your characters preferred method of feeding which most characters will have, but you can feed in other ways.<br /> <br /> As for the consensualist element, there's a few different ways to play it. You could say you need a blood donation, you could outright ask to drink from people, you could play it up as a kink thing. Of course, the ethics of getting consent and then dominating away their memory of doing it does make it a bit more ethically murky but I could see an argument for allowing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could include the I agree to have my memory erased provision in your initial compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:19:22-07:00","id":1378855,"title":"","content":"A Consensualist feeder probably has a stable of ghouls he or she feeds from. Alternatively, he or she might have someone close to him or her who knows the truth: a massive Masquerade breach, yes, but let's not fool ourselves and pretend this isn't a common trope in vampire stories. One of the NPCs in <i>Chicago By Night </i>has a wife who knows he's a vampire, and from whom he feeds almost exclusively. Honestly, there's a lot of Consensualists who could be Cleavers, and vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:24:18-07:00","id":1378856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1378782#post1378782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Consensualist&quot; is a major redflag for a Masquerade breach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you choose to be a Consensualist, you gain Dark Secret (Serial Masquerade Breacher). The Camarilla doesn't exactly approve of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:47:51-07:00","id":1378863,"title":"","content":"My question is actually feeding from Ghouls- is that really consensual? Because at that point their basically willed to give you their blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:27:35-07:00","id":1378878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere#post1378719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a Tremere [...] with a goodish personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? How did that slip through the vetting of the Tremere? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T20:52:32-07:00","id":1378916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1378863#post1378863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is actually feeding from Ghouls- is that really consensual? Because at that point their basically willed to give you their blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could be yes but not always, They could have been consenting before they feed from you several times. it takes four months for you to form a full bond if you haven't feed them more often than once a month. plenty of time to get consent. Other ways to feed.<br /> <br /> 1. you are a doctor that takes blood donations and try to convince people wherever you go to donate blood. You would need Iron Gullet to drink the blood if it is cold, rancid or fractionated plasma but nothing stops you from drinking somewhat fresh blood from a donor after they leave the area that you extracted it from them. They gave it willingly and you are happy to take it.<br /> <br /> 2. You are into kinky sex and higher prostitutes that are into role play, Dracula is your favorite.<br /> <br /> 3. You travel with two nurses/ mortal acolytes who are trusted and they just happen to know your secret and how to keep their mouths shut. you are Tremere and this happens more often that one would think. You should buy this as retainers and herd. Remember Tremere will take mortals that are promising and train them to see if they have what it takes.<br /> <br /> 4. You feed from consenting Vampires, though this is closer to blood leech you don't exclusively feed form them. So long as the blood has been out of their body for a few seconds it looses its power to bond you. Not only is a red solo cup your friend you are not breaching the masquerade and can gain access to several disciplines this way. At one point in time you probably did breach and will again so the flaw would stay.<br /> <br /> 5. Variation on the Blood donors, you require blood transfusions on a regular bases and collect blood from several people in your travels to keep you alive and doing your important work.<br /> <br /> All in all there are more than this but this should get you started or at least hopefully kick your imagination into gear. I would brush up the manipulation persuasion roll to keep the blood flowing though. Never neglect you feeding rolls, Feeding is at the core of a Vampires desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-06-2020, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:50:40-07:00","id":1379129,"title":"","content":"Predator Types describe different phenomena, with the result of overlap and duplication. This makes them highly flexible.<br /> <br /> While most Predator Types describe how a vampire puts fang to neck, &quot;Consensualist&quot; is about the mindset of the vessels. If the vessel gives consent (Which is a complex, complex, complex, and... did I mention complex?... <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consent\" target=\"_blank\">topic</a>.), the feeding itself can be accomplished through the methods of nearly any PT. If there are sexual overtones, it is Siren. If among friends and family, Cleaver. If the vessel is a vampire, Blood Leech. If in the context of a fight club, Alleycat. If in a house full of junkies, who let you feed on them while they are passed out, you have Sandman.<br /> <br /> You could choose nearly any other PT with the background note that the vampire prefers to gain consent. Is there a particular mechanical reason you specifically chose Consensualist and Scene Queen as your top two? If you're not doing it for a specific discipline or background, I would advise you to look elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <u>Consensualist's</u> most distinctive element is the free dot of Humanity. The problem is, this can be lost very easily. With one bad roll, you can lose the most distinctive thing you got from the PT.<br /> <br /> Plus, Prey Exclusion is a rough, rough flaw to play. If you feed without consent, you gain stains... which makes it more likely you will lose that dot of Humanity. You might also gain stains simply for observing other kindred feeding on the non-consenting. This could make your character rather disruptive of hunting for other pcs, as well as making attendance at vampire social events difficult.<br /> <br /> That is, of course, if you ever get invited to anything, considering you have Dark Secret (masquerade breaker). Understand the mechanics of Dark Secret. It is actually the Infamy flaw, except because it is not known it has a reduced value... in this case 1 dot. So, once revealed... and given you must spend a good chunk of your time scolding others for not getting consent when they feed to avoid Stains, it will be revealed... it becomes a 2 point infamy (masquerade breaker). This gives you a 2 dice penalty on all pertinent social rolls, which is a best-case scenario. In the Camarilla, this likely means a blood hunt.<br /> <br /> Note, Consensualist gives you the Dark Secret (masquerade breaker) flaw, which reveals to a 2 dot Infamy flaw. However, the Fame background specifically mentions &quot;serial breacher of the masquerade&quot; to be a two point secret, and thus a 3 dot Infamy. V5... sigh... gotta love it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <u>Scene Queen</u> is less weird, mechanically.<br /> <br /> Except, for one big thing. The flaw Prey Exclusion (a different subculture from your own).<br /> <br /> Okay, this might make sense if what you're trying to say is, &quot;My character is an academic, and wants to feed on academics.&quot; Except, that's not what the flaw does. It makes it so you gain Stains for feeding on non-academics, because... you... ummm... think anybody other than academics are evil and need to be fed on to reduce their population? Or, maybe, academics are so wonderful they... what... purify you as you feed?<br /> <br /> Plus, the flaw (per RAW rules, V5 p181) allows the ST to give you Stains for allowing anyone else to feed on your excluded vessels. So, if your Prey Exclusion is &quot;anyone who is not an academic&quot;, you risk getting stains for allowing a fellow player's pc to feed on a pedophile, unless, of course, the pedophile happens to have a PhD. In which case, dig in!<br /> <br /> Or, does the flaw mean you select &quot;a subculture other than your own&quot; in the sense that if your subculture is &quot;academics&quot;, your must choose a prey exclusion for a single other subculture, like &quot;bikers&quot; or &quot;aristocrats&quot;? If so, why would being a leader of one scene necessarily pit you against another subculture?<br /> <br /> If your chosen vessels are a different specific subculture (like an academic who refuses to feed on anyone who isn't a biker), you get the weird situation where you stridently campaign for the entire coterie to only feed from this other, unrelated subculture. This would be roleplayed as, &quot;Hey, my vampire friends, I know we all need to feed. I really must insist you only ever feed on bikers, because I am an academic. I will not allow any feeding on non-bikers!&quot;<br /> <br /> So... my suggestion would be avoid Consensualist.<br /> <br /> Scene Queen, maybe, is fine if you don't choose prey exclusion. Though this still leaves you with Disliked... and, really, why would every single person who isn't an academic dislike you?<br /> <br /> Have you considered Cleaver (representing that you have maintained your social ties in the university)? Or, Bagger (representing access to blood stores at the university's medical school or research labs)? Or, Osiris (representing what a dynamic and brilliant academic your pc is... take &quot;lectures&quot; as your entertainment specialty)? For that matter, take Sandman to represent access to the undergrad dorms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:00:28-07:00","id":1379133,"title":"","content":"Remember that humanity 8 gives you a re-roll on blush of life meaning that your hunger economy is better for it. And Don't do things that get you stains and you will be fine. Unless you have a vindictive GM that goes out of his way to Stain you, just don't do things that will give you stains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T20:33:44-07:00","id":1379167,"title":"","content":"Consensualists are for people who only want to take from humans voluntarily, probably for moral reasons.<br /> <br /> So no Disciplines or Ghouldom.<br /> <br /> However, it's like a heroin shot combined with the BEST SEX EVER so it's not like most humans wouldn't agree to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T10:19:09-07:00","id":1379269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1379129#post1379129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, does the flaw mean you select &quot;a subculture other than your own&quot; in the sense that if your subculture is &quot;academics&quot;, your must choose a prey exclusion for a single other subculture, like &quot;bikers&quot; or &quot;aristocrats&quot;? If so, why would being a leader of one scene necessarily pit you against another subculture?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I interpreted it. And it's up to the player to choose subcultures that make it make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1379129#post1379129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your chosen vessels are a different specific subculture (like an academic who refuses to feed on anyone who isn't a biker), you get the weird situation where you stridently campaign for the entire coterie to only feed from this other, unrelated subculture. This would be roleplayed as, &quot;Hey, my vampire friends, I know we all need to feed. I really must insist you only ever feed on bikers, because I am an academic. I will not allow any feeding on non-bikers!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that's just nonsense. You could try to take a ridiculous Prey Exclusion (or Feeding Restriction) in V20 and earlier too, and it's up to the ST to say &quot;you need to justify only feeding in bikers somehow&quot;.<br /> <br /> Same with the Ventrue clan bane. Mechanically, nothing stops an academic Ventrue from only being able to feed on bikers. But thematically that should have some kind of justification behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T13:52:24-07:00","id":1379316,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd recomend for anyone playing Tremere is to actually look up <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermeticism\" target=\"_blank\">Hermetic Theory</a> to understand the philosophy of Tremere. Does being a consensualist actually lie up with that world view? If not, how can I make a struggle out of it? (it's also fascinating stuff and it's great to ground your magic in a paradigm you're comfortable talking about)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T03:51:51-07:00","id":1380345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1378719-predator-question-how-to-be-a-consensualist-as-a-tremere?p=1379316#post1379316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'd recomend for anyone playing Tremere is to actually look up <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermeticism\" target=\"_blank\">Hermetic Theory</a> to understand the philosophy of Tremere. Does being a consensualist actually lie up with that world view? If not, how can I make a struggle out of it? (it's also fascinating stuff and it's great to ground your magic in a paradigm you're comfortable talking about)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hermeticism is a good idea to read about even if not playing a Tremere, but yes it is especially relevant if playing one. It is however a sprawling philosophy with many branches and it is easy to adhere to it and find support for different personal moral choices, particularly if it comes to moral choices regarding your and other persons true will.<br /> Also add Gnosticism to the reading list as several groups in vampire have their philosophy/faith based in that. Of course it is a good chance that reading about Hermetic Theory will lead you there anyway. Within Gnosticism you also have Sufism which will give you a good inroad to for example muslim Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25843-heliodromus","name":"Heliodromus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T13:10:38-07:00","id":1401176,"title":"","content":"Do it like the one in my chronic. Get yourself a mage Boy/Girlfriend that transforms water to blood for him/her or heals himself whenever (s)he whas getting sucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}